&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brief info about Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our mission is to make second-hand the first choice, and we&#39;re looking for people who want to help us get there. Every day, we work together to help our members buy and sell pre-loved clothing and lifestyle items, giving each piece a second life – or even a third. &lt;br&gt;The Vinted Group is made up of three business units that support this mission:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/marketplace&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Vinted Marketplace&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; is Europe’s leading platform for second-hand fashion and a go-to destination for all kinds of pre-loved items, with a growing range of categories. Our platform connects millions of members across 20+ markets, helping great items find a new life.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedgo&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Go&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; enhances the shipping experience with a vast network of over 500,000 pick-up and drop-off points, partnering with more than 60 carriers across Europe, with added services like item verification for peace of mind on high-value pieces.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedpay&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Pay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is the newest part of the Vinted Group, dedicated to bringing secure, reliable payments to buyers and sellers across Europe. Seamlessly integrated into the Vinted app, it helps keep every transaction safe, efficient, and easy for our members.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2008 in Lithuania, Vinted began as a way for friends to find new homes for clothes they no longer needed. In 2019, we became Lithuania&#39;s first unicorn! Today, our headquarters remain in Vilnius, and we&#39;ve grown with offices across Europe, supported by a team of over 2,000 people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Information about the position&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vinted&#39;s business has grown roughly 50% a year, and our infrastructure has to be ready for 10x today&#39;s transaction volume by 2030. It means modernizing how we build, provision, and run infrastructure, with automation and self-service replacing tickets and manual work. We need a &lt;strong&gt;Sr. TPM&lt;/strong&gt; to own the program that makes it happen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The 10x Scale program starts in Foundations, the domain that runs Vinted&#39;s data centers, compute, traffic routing, and cloud. It spans hardware and network provisioning, Kubernetes lifecycle automation, hybrid on-prem and cloud clusters, persistent workloads on Kubernetes, network capacity across data centers, and workload rightsizing. Scope is expanding: reaching 10x also depends on Platform, Security, and the product domains whose services run on this infrastructure. You&#39;ll be the person who connects all of it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want a multi-year program with real technical depth, hard numbers, and visibility at engineering leadership level, this is the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this position, you’ll&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Infrastructure for 10x scale program end to end: turn the target state into a multi-year roadmap with milestones, owners, and outcome metrics, and keep it current as the business and architecture evolve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run a portfolio of 15+ initiatives across compute, data center, network, cloud and other teams, managing the dependencies between them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow the program beyond Foundations: bring Platform, Security, and product domains into scope, agree what each must deliver, and make those commitments visible in their own plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the measurement layer: baseline and track provisioning lead time, share of requests fulfilled without manual work, cluster utilization, cost per transaction, and SLO attainment, and use them to drive decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive adoption on the consumer side: workload migrations to Kubernetes (including databases, Kafka, and other stateful services), rightsizing and autoscaling, migrating tools to cloud, move from tickets to self-service APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the long-lead work: hardware and network purchases, vendor and data center timelines, and the budget that goes with them, so capacity lands before demand does&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the program rhythm: weekly sync, planning, monthly business reviews, risk registers, and clear escalation of trade-offs to engineering leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the single source of truth on program status for engineering leadership and executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience in technical program management, with a proven track record of leading large-scale, cross-functional infrastructure programs end to end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background in SRE, infrastructure, or platform engineering, or engineering management in those areas, that gives you real technical credibility with the teams you&#39;ll work with&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in computer science, engineering, or a similar discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of compute, network infrastructure, data center and public cloud&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine bias for outcomes over outputs: you set success metrics before you start and measure consistently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running programs that mix software delivery with infrastructure and physical-world lead times: hardware procurement, vendor contracts, data center buildout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to drive accountability across teams and domains without direct authority, including at director and engineering leadership level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable leading in ambiguity and building the playbook as scope grows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication for both engineers and executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
